---

<section id="how-it-works" class="py-20 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
  <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-center text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-50">
    How to Format YAML Online
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-center text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Three simple steps to transform messy YAML into clean, properly-indented code.</p>
  <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-10">
    {[
      { step: '1', title: 'Paste or Upload Your YAML', desc: 'Copy your YAML from any source — a configuration file, a CI/CD pipeline, or a Kubernetes manifest — and paste it into the left editor panel. Alternatively, drag and drop a .yaml or .yml file from your computer. The editor supports files of any size, from a few lines to thousands.' },
      { step: '2', title: 'Format and Validate Instantly', desc: 'Our formatter processes your YAML locally in your browser using a YAML 1.2 compliant parser. It normalizes indentation, fixes spacing inconsistencies, and checks for syntax errors — all in milliseconds. The output panel updates in real-time as you type, or you can press Ctrl+Enter to trigger formatting manually. Use the indent selector (2, 4, or 8 spaces) to match your project conventions.' },
      { step: '3', title: 'Copy, Convert, or Compare', desc: 'Once your YAML is formatted, use the Copy button to grab the clean output. Switch to the YAML to JSON tab to convert your document for API consumption. The status bar confirms your YAML is valid with a green indicator, and shows line count and file size at a glance.' },
    ].map(({step, title, desc}) => (
      <div class="relative text-center">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center w-12 h-12 rounded-2xl bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-900/40 text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300 font-bold text-lg mb-5">{step}</span>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-lg">{title}</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">{desc}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>
